cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If SynVoy contributes to your research, please cite it as below."
title: "SynVoy: Synteny-guided orthology discovery"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Weitz
    given-names: Frank Andreas
  - family-names: Koludarov
    given-names: Ivan
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-21
repository-code: "https://github.com/AndreasWz/SynVoy"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  SynVoy finds the orthologs of a gene that is too divergent or too short for a
  genome-wide sequence search. It locates the gene's neighbouring genes in each
  target genome, where their order is conserved, and searches for the gene only
  inside that region. The target genomes need no annotation.
keywords:
  - synteny
  - orthology
  - comparative genomics
  - gene finding
  - Nextflow
